{"seq":3,"slug":"government-expenditure","title":"第三章 政府支出与预算","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-expenditure","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"public-spending-theory","title":"大学财政学 — 公共支出理论与增长规律","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-expenditure/public-spending-theory","wordCount":1645,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"social-security-transfers","title":"大学财政学 — 社会保障与转移支付","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-expenditure/social-security-transfers","wordCount":1695,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"budget-and-cost-benefit","title":"大学财政学 — 政府预算与成本收益分析","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-expenditure/budget-and-cost-benefit","wordCount":1590,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"第三章-政府支出与预算\">第三章 政府支出与预算</h1><p>收上来的钱要花出去，本章关注的就是&quot;钱花到哪里、花得值不值&quot;。我们先讨论公共支出的理论与增长规律（瓦格纳法则），再深入社会保障与转移支付这一现代政府最大的支出板块，理解养老金、医保和社会救助背后的经济逻辑与可持续性挑战。</p>\n<p>最后我们走进政府预算的&quot;操作间&quot;：预算如何编制、有哪些预算模式，以及如何用成本收益分析这把尺子去衡量一个公共项目（比如修一条地铁）到底值不值得投资。</p>\n"}